  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nLittle change in the overall pattern expected through much of the \nforecast period as South Texas remains under the influence of mid-\nlevel ridging. Sufficient moisture will remain in place for isolated \nshowers and thunderstorms to develop again on Thursday, mainly\nacross the southern half of the CWA. We may see a little better\nshot at some sea breeze showers and storms later this weekend into\nearly next week as the high shifts southwest with a slight increase\nin mid-level lift overspreading the region.\n\nAbove-normal temperatures will continue through the period, with hot \nafternoons and warm overnight lows expected. Heat index values will \ngenerally remain below 110 degrees, though locally higher values \ncannot be ruled out. Continue to practice heat safety when spending \ntime outdoors. \n\nForecast uncertainty begins to increase toward the middle of next \nweek as guidance hints at a possible disturbance approaching the \nregion. Confidence remains too low at this time regarding its \nevolution and potential impacts to South Texas.",
